@page "/admin/adoptions"
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "AdministratorOrInstitutionalAdmin")]
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
  Curriculum adoptions' old address, kept only so an old link or bookmark lands somewhere (T392, flow 15, Q1, S21): adoption
  is on Curricula now, in its "Open for adoption" section (the Administrator's in "An institution's curricula"), so this
  sends there, replacing itself in the history, and draws nothing. Its policy is kept, so a visitor who is signed out is
  sent to sign in, as before. Until T392 it was a page of its own: a picker that offered the version already adopted
  (which Adopt then refused), an adoption history, and the exception's text on a failure.
*@
@* The tab names where it lands, for the moment before the redirect does (T190). *@
<PageTitle>Curricula · Wombat</PageTitle>

@code {
  protected override void OnInitialized() => Navigation.NavigateTo(CatalogueLinks.Curricula, replace: true);
}
